{"post_stream":{"posts":[{"id":497417,"name":"Timothy Gresh","username":"Timothy_Gresh","avatar_template":"https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/t/ce7236/{size}.png","created_at":"2026-09-21T19:32:49.712Z","cooked":"\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-497417-where-does-the-bug-appear-featureproduct-1\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-497417-where-does-the-bug-appear-featureproduct-1\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eWhere does the bug appear (feature/product)?\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eGrok Bot\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-497417-describe-the-bug-2\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-497417-describe-the-bug-2\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eDescribe the Bug\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003ch2\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-497417-describe-the-bug-3\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-497417-describe-the-bug-3\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eDescribe the Bug\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eRegistered local computer shows connected. Light Shell works for hours when idle. When agents run heavier local work — especially CopyFromBox of a PowerShell script into %TEMP% then Shell that focuses Chrome (Win32 SetForegroundWindow + F5 for Mindbody keep-alive) or QBP browser automation — ListMachines flips to disconnected and the Grok Bot window vanishes. No Application Error / WER crash dump. Sentry queue empty. Full uninstall + delete install folder + fresh install from x.ai/bot did not fix. Over-the-top reinstall of 0.57.1 did not fix.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-497417-steps-to-reproduce-4\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-497417-steps-to-reproduce-4\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eSteps to Reproduce\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003ch2\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-497417-pattern-5\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-497417-pattern-5\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003ePattern\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003col\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eIdle / light hostname Shell: OK (observed 3+ hour continuous session after clean reinstall)\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eCopyFromBox + longer Shell / Chrome UI automation: dies within seconds; window gone\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eStartup relaunches app → open→die loop until full reboot + reinstall calmed idle path\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eChrome itself briefly flashed then closed once when app died mid-automation\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ol\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-497417-expected-behavior-6\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-497417-expected-behavior-6\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eExpected Behavior\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eLight Shell should remain stable for hours when idle, and heavier local work—especially CopyFromBox followed by Shell and Chrome UI automation—should complete without ListMachines disconnecting or the Grok Bot window vanishing. Chrome should remain available for the requested automation.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-497417-operating-system-7\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-497417-operating-system-7\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eOperating System\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWindows 10/11\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-497417-version-information-8\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-497417-version-information-8\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eVersion Information\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eVersion: Grok Bot 0.57.1 x64 — \u003ccode\u003eC:\\Users\\greshfit\\AppData\\Local\\Programs\\Grok Bot\\\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-497417-additional-information-9\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-497417-additional-information-9\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eAdditional Information\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eTitle:\u003c/strong\u003e Grok Bot 0.57.1 Windows — app quits under local Shell/CopyFromBox + Chrome UI; idle stays up\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eWhere:\u003c/strong\u003e Grok Bot desktop (Windows)\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eOS:\u003c/strong\u003e Windows 11 (10.0.26200), machine hostname SERVICE, Intel i5-8500T, ~16GB RAM, Wi-Fi only, Windows Defender only (no third-party AV)\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch2\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-497417-what-we-already-tried-10\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-497417-what-we-already-tried-10\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eWhat we already tried\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eConfirmed Windows sleep/hibernate/display Never on AC (not a PC power issue; last OS reboot was Windows Update Sep 16 before today’s reboot)\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eClean uninstall + delete Programs\\Grok Bot + reinstall 0.57.1\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003ePaused Mindbody keep-alive that CopyFromBox’d scripts to Temp\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eRedirected user TMP/TEMP to \u003ccode\u003e%LOCALAPPDATA%\\\\Grok Bot\\\\tmp\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eDefender ExclusionPath add failed (non-admin shell)\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eFiled Help → Send Feedback from the app (privacy mode blocked agent SendFeedback)\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003ch2\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-497417-related-reports-we-found-11\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-497417-related-reports-we-found-11\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eRelated reports we found\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003ccode\u003eforum.cursor.com\u003c/code\u003e: “temporarily unreachable” on Windows (AV scanning Temp ps-scripts, 10s timeout)\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003ccode\u003eforum.cursor.com\u003c/code\u003e: leftover local-exec-daemon after quit/relaunch\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003ccode\u003eforum.cursor.com\u003c/code\u003e: connected but file I/O unusable; timeout removes machine ~1 min\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eX: users hitting Windows tray Quit vs X-close leaving daemons (Grok replied with Task Manager cleanup)\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003ch2\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-497417-ask-12\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-497417-ask-12\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c